# winter — candidate palette, same derivation as cool.env:
# matplotlib's `winter` colormap sampled at t = 0, .25, .5, .75, 1 and
# pastelised toward white at strength 0.68; the alert pair at 0.25. The dark
# neutrals carry the ramp's own hue so the palette reads as one family.
COOL_BG0=#0E1B21
COOL_BG1=#1C2D35
COOL_BG2=#2A3E49
COOL_FG0=#EDF6FB
COOL_FG1=#ADD6EB
COOL_DIM=#8CC6E2
COOL_DIMMER=#73B9DC
COOL_0=#ADADFF
COOL_1=#ADC2F5
COOL_2=#ADD6EB
COOL_3=#ADEBE0
COOL_4=#ADFFD6
COOL_HOT_0=#4040FF
COOL_HOT_4=#40FF9F
COOL_MINT=#ADC2F5
COOL_BLUSH=#ADEBE0
COOL_ACCENT=#ADADFF
COOL_ACTIVE=#4040FF
COOL_URGENT=#40FF9F
COOL_WARN=#ADEBE0
COOL_GOOD=#ADC2F5
COOL_INACTIVE=#2A3E49
